Track 2: What Did The Joystick Say
- Story & Context: Sarah stands amidst the graveyard of glowing screens, pressing a broken arcade button until her thumb bleeds to get the machine to talk back. She confesses to the hardware that she’s tired of waiting for the power grid to acknowledge her existence, demanding a signal that isn't just static. "Tell me you were alive before the mall turned off," she pleads, her voice caught in a loop of digital stuttering as the PAD MM Dark Sleep swells grow until they swallow the percussion entirely.
